abstract: >-
  Research software and derived-data reproduction materials for a three-layer
  rolling-decision information attribution protocol, evaluated in Australian
  storage arbitrage with local learning and partial Ontario comparator/replay
  checks. Core v10 scientific outputs and v11 figure design are distinguished
  from supplementary diagnostics added during the v13 revision, including
  20 completed stricter-clock replays reported as point sensitivity without
  new confidence intervals. Inference is
  conditional on retained programs and observed history; scoped internal fresh
  execution is not independent external replication of the whole study.
  Original software is MIT licensed; third-party data retain separate terms.
